# Root-lane counts for `-p delphi-runtime --tests`, ALL 17 targets under sudo.
#
# LANE RUN 19 — **the first root execution of the daemon's shutdown policy.** Measured
# 2026-09-07 at `c10810f`.
#
#   EXECUTED 216 / SKIPPED 5 / reported 221     extractor rc=0
#   producers: 17/17 exited 0                   failures: 0
#   predicted 216/5/221 at c10810f, committed ALONE and BEFORE the run — and MATCHED EXACTLY
#   membership: root 221 identities / unpriv 221, ZERO in either direction, rc 0
#
# All eight `shutdown::tests` ran at root and are quoted by name in the transcript:
#   a_child_that_outlives_the_grace_period_is_killed_and_reaped              ok
#   a_cooperating_child_is_reaped_within_grace_with_its_status_preserved     ok
#   a_pid_that_is_not_our_child_terminates_the_policy_promptly               ok
#   an_already_reaped_child_is_reported_gone_without_waiting                 ok
#   children_are_shut_down_independently_and_each_outcome_is_attributed      ok
#   non_positive_pids_are_refused_rather_than_signalling_a_group             ok
#   only_an_unreaped_child_counts_as_failed_cleanup                          ok
#   the_daemon_delegates_shutdown_and_does_not_reap_by_hand                  ok
#
# That closes a gap that stood for THREE rounds (D0A-R28-02 → R29-05 → run 18), in which the
# policy was compiled, linked, and run PAST rather than THROUGH.
#
# =========================================================================================
# THE TWO PREDICTIONS ABOUT WHAT THIS RUN COULD SHOW — BOTH HELD, AND BOTH LIMIT THE CLAIM
# =========================================================================================
#
# **1. THE DELEGATION GUARD PASSED AT ROOT AND THAT ADDS NOTHING.** Said before the run, and
# it is the honest reading rather than a hedge:
# `the_daemon_delegates_shutdown_and_does_not_reap_by_hand` uses `include_str!` — it reads
# `bin/delphi-runtimed.rs` **at compile time** and asserts on its text. It executes no process
# and touches no privilege, so running it as root re-checks a string already checked.
#
# What it establishes in either lane is real and was earned: `main` calls `shutdown_all` and
# carries no second copy of the policy. It **caught one** on its first run — `ChildReaper::Drop`
# had its own kill-and-bounded-reap, now routed through the same implementation with a ZERO
# grace, so the two paths differ in an ARGUMENT rather than in code.
#
# **What run 19 does NOT show is that `main`'s branch is TAKEN at root after a terminal
# outcome.** That is ASSEMBLY coverage, it is owed, and the only root exercise of that binary —
# `b1_daemon_binary_runs_the_assembled_flow` — still SKIPS for want of
# `--features insecure-test-seams`. Do not read a green delegation guard as evidence about the
# root call site.
#
# **2. THE PER-CHILD ATTRIBUTION CASES PASSED *IDENTICALLY*, WHICH IS NOT THE SAME AS ROOT
# *COVERING* THEM.** `children_are_shut_down_independently_and_each_outcome_is_attributed`
# spawns its OWN children (`sh -c exit 0`, `sleep 120`) and reaps them, and **reaping or
# signalling your own children requires no privilege** — so root was predicted to behave exactly
# as unprivileged, and did.
#
# The correct record is therefore **IDENTICAL, not COVERED**. These fixtures establish
# SAME-CREDENTIAL child cleanup and nothing wider: root's extra signalling power is over
# processes with different credentials, which is what production's PRIVILEGE-DROPPED children
# are and what no fixture here constructs. A difference would have been a result worth stopping
# for; sameness is the expected outcome and carries no extra assurance.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A SAFETY CHANGE MADE BEFORE THIS RUN — AND ITS JUSTIFICATION WAS PARTLY WRONG (D0A-R30-06)
#
# `a_pid_that_is_not_our_child` named **pid 1** and was changed to `pid_max` at `0cf555e`
# before this run. **Keeping unrelated system processes out of fixtures is right and the change
# stands.** The REASONING recorded for it was not:
#
#   * IT SAID `kill(1, SIGKILL)` AT ROOT ENDS INIT. **It does not.** Linux gives PID 1 special
#     protection: a signal with no handler installed by PID 1 is not delivered to it, SIGKILL
#     included. The dramatic version of the hazard was invented, and it was written into a
#     document that exists to be trusted, unchecked, by me — and left standing by the operator.
#   * IT CONFUSED WAIT ELIGIBILITY WITH SIGNAL PERMISSION. Parenthood governs whether you may
#     `wait` for a process. It does not grant permission to signal one; that depends on
#     credentials and capabilities. The lane note reasoned from the wrong relation.
#
# **What the fixtures actually establish, stated at the right strength:** same-credential child
# cleanup. Every child here is spawned by the test process with its own credentials, so the
# result generalises to that case and no further. **Production's children are
# PRIVILEGE-DROPPED** (`delphi-drop`), which is a materially different signalling relationship
# and one these fixtures do not exercise at all. That gap closes through ASSEMBLY testing, not
# through running the same fixtures at root.
#
# This correction is recorded rather than the sentence quietly edited, because a false claim
# about a SAFETY property in the lane record is worse than the same claim anywhere else: the
# record is what a later reader trusts instead of re-deriving.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EVERY HYGIENE CHECK, WITH THE EVIDENCE THAT DECIDES IT
#
#   account          delphi-tool:x:997:972       (gid 972, not 997 — D0A-R17-02)
#   helper digest    aba0f0ea14b751aa…           INSTALLED == STAGED, both printed
#   bwrap            0.11.1
#   free space       /run 1483M, target 3375M, /tmp 3710M — all above floor
#   forced freshness ENFORCED: enumeration asserted at 17, BOTH hash sides asserted equal to
#                    17, rebuild failure fatal, `diff` empty.
#   PAM before       439c1d1521d86e4eb011a927aff659db
#   PAM after        md5sum -c → OK              (class 16, the defect already paid for)
#   stale sessions   none, checked before AND after
#
# **THE CORRECTED DISK MODEL HELD A SECOND TIME.** Run 17 3397M → run 18 3377M (−20M) → run 19
# 3375M (**−2M**). The "~0.5 GiB per lane run" figure I reported and carried into a prompt was
# wrong: the −506M it rested on spanned fourteen mutation-campaign rebuilds. Lane runs are
# cheap; campaigns are the expensive operation. Measure by OPERATION, not by wall-clock between
# runs.
#
# THE FIVE SKIPS, each quoting its own blocker: b1_daemon_binary (needs --features
# insecure-test-seams), an_unreadable_login_defs (this uid can read a 0000 file),
# pidfd_refuses_a_recycled_pid_barrier (no user namespaces), live_logind_query (standing DEFER),
# a_regular_login_user_is_not_refused (running as root). Three skip BECAUSE the run is
# privileged, so root's 216 and the unprivileged 196 are OVERLAPPING SETS.
#
# ORDERING HELD UNDER CONVENTION FOR THE SEVENTH CONSECUTIVE RUN (D0A-R22-01, still reopened).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT A GREEN RUN 19 STILL DOES NOT ESTABLISH
#
# 1. **Assembly coverage** of the daemon's exit path (above) — owed, and the reviewer named it
#    separately from the extraction.
# 2. **R29-05's `Unreaped` branch** needs a child in uninterruptible sleep; nothing constructs
#    one. `only_an_unreaped_child_counts_as_failed_cleanup` constructs the VALUE, not the
#    CONDITION.
# 3. **R29-06's EINTR retry** needs a signal delivered inside the `waitpid` window; nothing
#    delivers one.
# 4. The mutation campaign is unprivileged-only; the five root-gated tests have never been
#    mutation-tested.
# 5. The suspend divergence is unmeasured; `action.timeout` is enforced nowhere (R9-04).
#
